{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\007.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "1.2Primefactorization", "conf": 0.885, "box": [[684, 114], [1278, 99], [1279, 152], [685, 167]]}, {"text": "Prime factorization is a process in which a number is", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[479, 214], [1486, 194], [1487, 240], [480, 260]]}, {"text": "written as a product of its prime factors.", "conf": 0.936, "box": [[490, 278], [1236, 253], [1238, 306], [492, 331]]}, {"text": "PreviousKnowledge Check", "conf": 0.883, "box": [[1231, 417], [1715, 417], [1715, 457], [1231, 457]]}, {"text": "Example 1:", "conf": 0.87, "box": [[166, 481], [376, 475], [377, 519], [167, 525]]}, {"text": "What is meant by prime", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[1294, 498], [1659, 502], [1659, 537], [1294, 534]]}, {"text": "Find the prime factors of 60.", "conf": 0.882, "box": [[168, 546], [676, 537], [676, 580], [168, 588]]}, {"text": "factors?", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[1296, 547], [1417, 547], [1417, 582], [1296, 582]]}, {"text": "Solution:", "conf": 0.862, "box": [[170, 611], [344, 609], [344, 649], [170, 651]]}, {"text": "Step I:First we break 60 into its factors as:2× 30", "conf": 0.858, "box": [[632, 692], [1525, 676], [1526, 719], [633, 735]]}, {"text": "60", "conf": 0.588, "box": [[307, 706], [360, 706], [360, 750], [307, 750]]}, {"text": "Step II:Now we break 30 into its factors as:2 × 15", "conf": 0.876, "box": [[633, 757], [1550, 742], [1550, 785], [633, 800]]}, {"text": "30", "conf": 0.618, "box": [[309, 771], [363, 771], [363, 816], [309, 816]]}, {"text": "Step Ill: Now we break 15 into its factors as: 3 × 5", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[634, 822], [1547, 807], [1548, 853], [635, 868]]}, {"text": "15", "conf": 0.645, "box": [[314, 838], [365, 838], [365, 884], [314, 884]]}, {"text": "As 3 and 5 are prime numbers,so we stop here.", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[636, 884], [1496, 878], [1496, 923], [636, 929]]}, {"text": "60=2×30", "conf": 0.728, "box": [[271, 1001], [480, 999], [480, 1036], [271, 1038]]}, {"text": "Noteitdown", "conf": 0.871, "box": [[1263, 1008], [1496, 1008], [1496, 1045], [1263, 1045]]}, {"text": "= 2 ×2 ×15", "conf": 0.739, "box": [[319, 1065], [539, 1062], [539, 1099], [319, 1103]]}, {"text": "Theorderoffactorizationdoes", "conf": 0.95, "box": [[1264, 1089], [1726, 1087], [1726, 1119], [1264, 1121]]}, {"text": "=2×2×3×5", "conf": 0.71, "box": [[321, 1131], [586, 1126], [586, 1162], [321, 1166]]}, {"text": "notaffectprimefactorization.", "conf": 0.944, "box": [[1263, 1136], [1707, 1132], [1707, 1165], [1263, 1169]]}, {"text": "The prime factorization of 60 = 2 ×2 ×3 × 5.", "conf": 0.843, "box": [[196, 1196], [1003, 1185], [1003, 1229], [196, 1240]]}, {"text": "Example 2:", "conf": 0.837, "box": [[199, 1324], [412, 1321], [412, 1365], [199, 1367]]}, {"text": "Find prime factors of 120 by factor tree method.", "conf": 0.9, "box": [[200, 1389], [1073, 1374], [1074, 1416], [201, 1431]]}, {"text": "Step I: First we break 120 into its factors as: 10 and 12", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[835, 1453], [1802, 1440], [1802, 1484], [835, 1498]]}, {"text": "120", "conf": 0.625, "box": [[485, 1468], [558, 1465], [559, 1507], [486, 1510]]}, {"text": "Step Il: Now we break 10 into its factors as: 2 × 5", "conf": 0.907, "box": [[838, 1516], [1719, 1505], [1719, 1550], [838, 1560]]}, {"text": "Step Ill: Now we break 12 into its factors as: 3 × 4", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[841, 1579], [1730, 1571], [1730, 1614], [841, 1622]]}, {"text": "10", "conf": 0.665, "box": [[288, 1589], [336, 1589], [336, 1624], [288, 1624]]}, {"text": "12", "conf": 0.525, "box": [[647, 1589], [690, 1589], [690, 1620], [647, 1620]]}, {"text": "Step IV: Now we break 4 into its factors as: 2 × 2", "conf": 0.867, "box": [[844, 1642], [1714, 1635], [1714, 1679], [844, 1686]]}, {"text": "As the end factorsare all primes.So,we stop-here", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[846, 1704], [1733, 1704], [1733, 1746], [846, 1746]]}, {"text": "So, the prime factors of 120 are 2 × 2 × 2 × 3 × 5", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[220, 1901], [1089, 1875], [1090, 1918], [221, 1944]]}, {"text": "We can also write the prime factors of 120 as: 2 × 3 × 5", "conf": 0.915, "box": [[218, 1962], [1218, 1932], [1219, 1981], [219, 2010]]}, {"text": "Here 2\" is the representation of number in index notation.", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[222, 2022], [1268, 1996], [1269, 2044], [223, 2071]]}, {"text": "ING", "conf": 0.602, "box": [[284, 2143], [325, 2143], [325, 2161], [284, 2161]]}, {"text": "prime factors by using prime factorization and factor tree method.", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[379, 2197], [1335, 2170], [1336, 2213], [380, 2240]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.769, "box": [[323, 2344], [651, 2328], [653, 2367], [325, 2383]]}]}